# Qwen3.5-MoE — exact model math (implementation reference)

Derived from the authoritative HF `transformers` 5.12.1 reference
(`models/qwen3_5_moe/modeling_qwen3_5_moe.py`) and the actual checkpoint
tensor inventory. All engine kernels must reproduce this math bit-faithfully
(fp32 accumulation where the reference forces fp32).

## Config (35B-A3B / 122B-A10B)

| param | 35B | 122B |
|---|---|---|
| hidden_size | 2048 | 3072 |
| num_hidden_layers | 40 | 48 |
| layer pattern | 3× linear_attention : 1× full_attention (`full_attention_interval=4`; full at layer idx 3,7,11,…) | same |
| num_attention_heads / kv_heads | 16 / 2 | 32 / 2 |
| head_dim | 256 | 256 |
| partial_rotary_factor | 0.25 → rotary_dim=64 | same |
| rope_theta | 1e7 | same |
| linear_num_key_heads / value_heads | 16 / 32 | 16 / 64 |
| linear_key/value_head_dim | 128 | 128 |
| linear_conv_kernel_dim | 4 | 4 |
| num_experts / top-k | 256 / 8 | 256 / 8 |
| moe_intermediate_size | 512 | 1024 |
| shared_expert_intermediate_size | 512 | 1024 |
| vocab_size | 248320 | 248320 |
| rms_norm_eps | 1e-6 | 1e-6 |
| mtp_num_hidden_layers | 1 | 1 |

`tie_word_embeddings = false` (separate `lm_head.weight`).

## RMSNorm — TWO different conventions, do not mix

1. **`Qwen3_5MoeRMSNorm`** (input_layernorm, post_attention_layernorm, q_norm,
   k_norm, final norm, MTP norms) — **zero-centered weight**:
   `y = (x_f32 * rsqrt(mean(x²)+eps)) * (1.0 + w_f32)`, computed in fp32, cast
   to output dtype at the end. Checkpoint weights are near 0.
2. **`Qwen3_5MoeRMSNormGated`** (`linear_attn.norm`, per v-head over
   head_v_dim=128) — plain multiplicative weight + SiLU gate:
   `y = (rmsnorm(x_f32) * w) * silu(z_f32)`. Checkpoint weights near 1.

## Rotary (full-attention layers only)

- `inv_freq[j] = theta^(-2j/64)`, j=0..31. For text-only, all three mrope
  position streams are equal → interleaved-mrope reduces to standard RoPE.
- Partial: only dims `[0,64)` of the 256-dim head rotate; dims `[64,256)` pass
  through. Non-interleaved **rotate_half** convention on the 64-dim slice:
  `q[0:32] = q_rot[0:32]*cos - q_rot[32:64]*sin; q[32:64] = q_rot[32:64]*cos + q_rot[0:32]*sin`
  with `cos[i]=cos(pos*inv_freq[i%32])`.

## Full attention layer (gated attention)

```
q_full = q_proj(x)                       # [T, heads*2*256], NVFP4/FP8 quantized
per head h: q = q_full[h*512 :  h*512+256], gate = q_full[h*512+256 : h*512+512]
q = RMSNorm_zc(q) (per-head, 256, zero-centered w)   then partial RoPE
k = RMSNorm_zc(k_proj(x) per head)                   then partial RoPE
v = v_proj(x)
attn = softmax(q·kᵀ * 256^-0.5 + causal_mask) @ v    # GQA: kv head = h/8 (35B)
out  = attn * sigmoid(gate)              # elementwise, per head
y    = o_proj(out)                       # [heads*256 → hidden]
```
Softmax in fp32. KV cache per full-attn layer: 2 kv-heads × 256 × 2 tensors.

## Linear attention layer (gated DeltaNet)

Projections (all from same x): `qkv = in_proj_qkv(x)` → `[q:2048 | k:2048 | v:4096]`
(35B: 16 k-heads×128, 16 q... q uses key_dim as well: q,k both 16×128, v 32×128);
`z = in_proj_z(x)` → 4096; `b = in_proj_b(x)` → 32; `a = in_proj_a(x)` → 32.
All these are **bf16 unquantized** in both checkpoints.

Causal depthwise conv1d (channels = 8192, K=4, **no bias**), state = last 4
raw qkv vectors (pre-conv, incl. current):
```
conv_state: ring of K vectors [8192]
decode step: push qkv_t; y[c] = Σ_{j=0..3} state[c][j] * w[c][j]; qkv_t = silu(y)
```

Per-token gates (fp32): `beta = sigmoid(b)` [32]; `g = -exp(A_log) * softplus(a + dt_bias)` [32].
(`A_log`, `dt_bias`: fp32 params [32].)

Head mapping: v-head i uses k/q-head `i / (num_v/num_k)` (repeat_interleave —
consecutive pairs share, 35B: v-heads 2i,2i+1 ← k-head i).

Decode recurrence per v-head (state S ∈ fp32[128 kdim][128 vdim]):
```
q = l2norm(q, eps=1e-6) * 128^-0.5      # NOTE: l2norm = x * rsqrt(sum(x²)+eps)  (sum, not mean)
k = l2norm(k, eps=1e-6)
S *= exp(g_head)
kv_mem[dv] = Σ_dk S[dk][dv] * k[dk]
delta[dv]  = (v[dv] - kv_mem[dv]) * beta_head
S[dk][dv] += k[dk] * delta[dv]
o[dv]      = Σ_dk S[dk][dv] * q[dk]
```
Then per v-head: `o = RMSNormGated(o, z_head)` (convention 2), concat heads,
`y = out_proj(o)` (4096→hidden, bf16).

Prefill: recurrence applied per token is exact (chunked UT-transform algorithm
in the reference is a mathematically identical speedup — optional later).
State per sequence: 32×128×128 fp32 = 2 MiB/layer, 30 layers = 60 MiB (35B).

## MoE block (every layer)

```
router_logits = x @ gate.weightᵀ         # [T,256], bf16 weight, fp32 logits
p = softmax_f32(router_logits)
top8 idx/vals; w_i = p_i / Σ_top8 p      # renormalize
routed = Σ_i w_i * down_i( silu(gate_i(x)) * up_i(x) )   # NVFP4/FP8 experts, 2048→512→2048
shared = down_s( silu(gate_s(x)) * up_s(x) )             # NVFP4/FP8, 2048→512→2048
y = routed + sigmoid(shared_expert_gate(x)) * shared     # shared_expert_gate: [1,2048] bf16
```

## Quantized weight decode

- **FP8 checkpoint** (verified via shard headers, Shifusen 122B):
  `weight F8_E4M3 [out,in]` + `weight_scale BF16 [out,1]` (per-channel; loader
  must accept bf16 or fp32 scales): `W[r][c] = fp8_decode(W[r][c]) * scale[r]`.
  Conv1d weight stored `[channels, 1, 4]`. 122B in_proj_qkv = 12288
  (2048 q + 2048 k + 8192 v), in_proj_z = 8192, q_proj out = 16384 (32h×2×256).
- **NVFP4 checkpoint** (verified against `compressed-tensors` 0.17.1
  `NVFP4PackedCompressor`): `weight_packed[out][in/2]` uint8 — **low nibble =
  even column, high nibble = odd column**; nibble = sign bit 0x8 | 3-bit index
  into `{0, .5, 1, 1.5, 2, 3, 4, 6}`. `weight_scale[out][in/16]` fp8_e4m3,
  `weight_global_scale` fp32 scalar. Dequant (exact reference semantics):
  `W[r][c] = e2m1(nibble) * ( fp8_decode(weight_scale[r][c/16]) / weight_global_scale )`.
  `input_global_scale` is for static activation quant — unused (we do
  dynamic/f32 activations).

### Checkpoint quantization coverage (35B NVFP4)

| tensors | format |
|---|---|
| routed experts gate/up/down (40×256×3) | NVFP4 |
| shared expert gate/up/down | NVFP4 |
| full-attn q/k/v/o_proj | NVFP4 |
| linear_attn in_proj_qkv/z/b/a, out_proj, conv1d, A_log, dt_bias, norms | bf16/fp32 |
